{
  "question_id": "q_018_alibaba_compressed_mean",
  "slug": "alibaba-compressed-mean",
  "title": "Compressed Mean",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "company": "Alibaba",
  "premium": false,
  "question": "You're trying to find the mean number of items per order on Alibaba, rounded to 1 decimal place using tables which includes information on the count of items in each order (item_count table) and the corresponding number of orders for each item count (order_occurrences table).",
  "notes": [
    "There are a total of 500 orders with one item per order, 1000 orders with two items per order, and 800 orders with three items per order.\"",
    "Let's calculate the arithmetic average:",
    "Total items = (1*500) + (2*1000) + (3*800) + (4*1000) = 8900",
    "Total orders = 500 + 1000 + 800 + 1000 = 3300",
    "Mean = 8900 / 3300 = 2.7",
    "The dataset you are querying against may have different input & output - this is just an example!"
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "items_per_order",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "item_count",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "order_occurrences",
          "data_type": "INT"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sample_data": {
    "items_per_order": [
      {
        "item_count": "1",
        "order_occurrences": "500"
      },
      {
        "item_count": "2",
        "order_occurrences": "1000"
      },
      {
        "item_count": "3",
        "order_occurrences": "800"
      },
      {
        "item_count": "4",
        "order_occurrences": "1000"
      }
    ]
  },
  "sample_output": [
    {
      "mean": "2.7"
    }
  ],
  "reference_sql": "SELECT \n  ROUND(SUM(item_count * order_occurrences) / SUM(order_occurrences), 1) AS mean\nFROM items_per_order;",
